dening in one quarter adds about 0.30 percentage points to new-issue yields, assuming base rates stay the same. That raises interest costs on the refinancing and new debt behind the 2027 capex plans.\n- **Access:** Debt markets are open. Norvane priced a C$1.1B bond \"comfortably\", which shows real demand for good credits at the wider spreads.\n- **Equity is weaker:** Two utility share offerings were cut back in size. Separately, Pellham Power withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering and scaled back 2027 transformer orders. Utilities will therefore lean more on debt, and wider spreads make that costlier.\n- **Outlook:** The trend is for debt to be available but more expensive. Weaker issuers may find access harder than Norvane did, and Pellham is the one to watch given its larger spending increase of 18%, against 12% for Norvane.\n\nI found no data on spreads by issuer, so I can't say how far the widening differs between Pellham and Norvane. I also don't know whether the widening continued into Q4.","ttft_ms":5473,"type":"result","duration_ms":14294,"uuid":"79b4dd3d-82f4-4cd6-90da-cb7d1db82365","ttft_stream_ms":4647,"time_to_request_ms":136,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":9,"system_prompt":10,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":6,"input_attachments":27,"input_hooks":6,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":16,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":10,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":6,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":23,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":30,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":62,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":187,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":113,"process_rss_mib_result":197,"process_anon_mib_result":116,"process_peak_rss_mib":197,"process_cpu_ms_turn":477,"process_wall_ms_turn":14291,"process_